**Company setup › Company profile** holds the facts about the company that the books depend on.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/setup-profile-company" caption="The company profile of ABC PTE. LTD." /%}

## Company Profile

The company's name, UEN, financial year end, base currency and GST settings. Operon reads these when it books and when it prepares the F5. Correct them here when they change.

## Bank accounts

The register of every bank, wallet and card account of the company, with the currency of each account. Each bank statement is attached to one registered account. When a statement arrives for an account that is not registered, Operon asks which account it belongs to.

An account that was opened during the period is confirmed on the bank reconciliation page (see [Step 2 · Reconcile: bank](/en/bookkeeping/reconcile-bank/)). The months before the opening date then need no statement.

## Employees

The payroll register. Operon uses it to recognise salaries, CPF and claims paid to staff. A payment to a person who is not on the register is raised as a to-do item.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/setup-profile-employees" caption="The payroll register with two fictional employees." /%}

## Related parties

Directors, shareholders and related companies. Record them here so that payments to and from them can be booked to the right party, for example to the amount due to a director.
